miniKanren with recursive bindings
==================================

mk.scm is William Byrd's miniKanren, as bundled with his
hindley-milner-type-inferencer (MIT, LICENSE beside this file), by way
of Hirotaka Niitsuma's Racket port of it:

    https://github.com/niitsuma/hindley-milner-type-inferencer

Four definitions in it -- ext-s-check, occurs-check, walk and walk* --
carry a change after Niitsuma's recursive miniKanren:

    Hirotaka Niitsuma, Context-Free Grammars Including Left Recursion
    using Recursive miniKanren, Computacion y Sistemas 22(4), 2018.
    https://doi.org/10.13053/cys-22-4-3072

Stock miniKanren refuses a self-referential binding: the occurs check
sees the variable inside the term it is being bound to and fails. Here
the binding is taken and annotated instead, as (==> x t), naming the
recursion rather than looping on it, and the three traversals carry the
variables they have already entered so that they terminate on a
substitution containing such a binding.

What this buys is recursive types. The type of a delayed stream
contains itself, and stock Hindley-Milner has no way to write it; with
this change it comes out as (==> T ...) and can be read as the nominal
recursive type the emitter already has. What it costs is that
self-application types as well, so the inferencer is no longer a filter
for that class of error.

Each changed definition is marked in mk.scm.
